<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Herman Willem Daendels</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1762–1818</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Herman Willem Daendels was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Patriot and general who served as governor-general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a> from 1808 to 1811 for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-bonaparte">Louis Bonaparte</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-holland">Kingdom of Holland</a>. To defend <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> he reorganised its administration, built the Great Post Road along the north coast with forced labour, and curbed the Javanese rulers, destroying the palace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banten">Banten</a>. He later governed the Dutch <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a>, where he died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/herman-willem-daendels.jpg" alt="Herman Willem Daendels" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raden Sarief Bastaman Saleh · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Posthuum_portret_van_Herman_Willem_Daendels_(1762-1818)._Gouverneur-generaal_(1808-10)_Rijksmuseum_SK-A-3790.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
